+## Optional: CompliR counterparty screening
+
+Set `COMPLIR_URL` to a [CompliR](https://github.com/mrnetwork0001/complir) host and `/api/contracts/validate-work` looks up the beneficiary's risk tier (`GET /api/v1/attestation/<address>`, free) before calling `withdraw`. A `HIGH` tier returns `403` and the funds stay in escrow; `LOW`/`MEDIUM` release as before, and an unreachable CompliR fails open with a warning. The same gate exists on-chain: `RefundProtocol.setComplir(registry)` makes `withdraw` and `earlyWithdrawByArbiter` revert with `CompliRTierTooHigh` for a `HIGH` recipient (`ICompliR.sol`, registry `0xA82EDb5e111c31C63E06EF0007f2fa1a9e7EB30d` on [Arc mainnet](https://explorer.arc.network/address/0xA82EDb5e111c31C63E06EF0007f2fa1a9e7EB30d)); recompile the contract and refresh `REFUND_PROTOCOL_BYTECODE` in `lib/constants.ts` to use it. For a fresh verdict with reasons and recommended limits, the paid `POST /api/v1/screen` (x402, 0.01 USDC on Arc) is the upgrade path.
+
